  "title": "Count each integer and write it back as many times as it occurs",
  "summary": "Use each value as an index to count its occurrences, then write the values back in increasing order.",
  "context": [
    "The input is nums = [1, 0, 1, 2, 0, 4, 0, 2, 2, 4]. Its values are nonnegative integers and its maximum is 4, so create a five-slot array counter with indices 0 through 4, where counter[num] counts occurrences of num. Its index represents the value itself, rather than a position in the input."
  ],
  "description": [
    "Here counter[3] = 0 means the input contains no 3. Read indices 0 through 4 and output three 0s, two 1s, three 2s, and two 4s, in that order. The three tables below give the input, frequencies, and array written back."
  ],
